657	export async function detectSilences(wavPath: string, o?: { noiseDb?: number; minSec?: number }): Promise<{ start: number; end: number }[]>
658	export function alignLines(lines: { id: string; text: string }[], totalSec: number, silences: { start: number; end: number }[]): LineTiming[]
659	export function estimateTimings(lines: { id: string; text: string }[]): LineTiming[]
660	export async function voiceLines(lines: { id: string; text: string }[], o: { provider: TtsProvider; voice: string; outDir: string; maxCalls: number }): Promise<{ mode: 'voiced' | 'captions'; audioPath: string | null; timings: LineTiming[]; calls: number }>
661	```
662	
663	Behaviour:
664	
665	- **One call per reel.** The free tier allows few generations per key per day, so all lines are sent as one text, joined by blank lines, prefixed with `Read as a calm, dry documentary narrator. Pause for a full second between paragraphs.\n\n`.
666	- **Gemini request.** `POST https://generativelanguage.googleapis.com/v1beta/models/<model>:generateContent`, header `x-goog-api-key`, body `{ contents: [{ parts: [{ text }] }], generationConfig: { responseModalities: ['AUDIO'], speechConfig: { voiceConfig: { prebuiltVoiceConfig: { voiceName } } } } }`. Audio is base64 16-bit mono PCM at `candidates[0].content.parts[0].inlineData.data`; the sample rate is the `rate=` value of `mimeType` (24000 when absent).
667	- **Rotation.** Models are tried in order `gemini-3.1-flash-tts-preview`, `gemini-3.8-flash-tts`, `gemini-2.5-flash-preview-tts`. HTTP 429 moves to the next key; when every key is exhausted for a model the next model is tried; when all fail `TtsQuotaError` is thrown. HTTP 5xx is retried twice with a 2 s wait.
668	- **`detectSilences`.** Runs `ffmpeg -i <wav> -af silencedetect=noise=<noiseDb>dB:d=<minSec> -f null -` (defaults -35 and 0.45) and parses `silence_start` / `silence_end` from stderr.
669	- **`alignLines`.** Drop silences touching the start or end of the audio. With `n` lines, `n - 1` boundaries are needed. The expected position of boundary `i` is `totalSec` times the cumulative share of characters up to line `i`. Each boundary takes the unused silence whose midpoint is nearest to its expected position and within 25% of `totalSec` of it; a boundary with no such silence uses the expected position. Line `i` runs from boundary `i - 1` to boundary `i` (0 and `totalSec` at the ends). The function never throws and always returns `n` contiguous, non-overlapping timings.
670	- **`estimateTimings`.** 15 characters per second, minimum 1.6 s per line, contiguous from zero.
671	- **`voiceLines`.** Uses a cached WAV under `outDir/cache/<sha256 of model list, voice and text>.wav` when present (zero calls). Otherwise synthesises, writes `outDir/narration.wav`, detects silences and aligns. On `TtsQuotaError`, or when `maxCalls` is zero, it returns `mode: 'captions'`, `audioPath: null` and `estimateTimings`.
